ttf-larabie (1:20011216-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The 'somehow I care less for non-free packages' release
  * Bump epoch to make package non-native
  * using debhelper v4

  * I tried using defoma again - but it's horribly slow!
    it takes more than three minutes to setup the deco font package
    on my 1.8 GHz laptop - that is not acceptable. Disabling defoma again.

  * Packages no longer include a fonts.scale file as used by earlier
    X11 versions. This shouldn't be needed anymore since Xfree 4.
  * Not using update-fonts-* any more either (Closes: #312058)
  * By not using ttmkfdir and fonts.scale any more, the fonts shouldn't
    pretend to support charsets they don't any more (Closes: #151757)

  * if fontconfig is installed, update it's cache
  * Add build-dep to unzip (Closes: #256400)

  * the renaming in the previous version (which was never uploaded
    due to speed issues with defoma) should fix the abiword filename
    issues (closes: #178297)

 -- Erich Schubert <erich@debian.org>  Wed,  5 Oct 2005 00:16:18 +0200

